            {
                "entry_id": "94ffef87-0412-3a8b-ada8-9792dcc40af9",
                "word": "cladistique",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "dc6c2bff-a1ac-4627-91f5-18e8ccd47547",
                        "entry_id": "94ffef87-0412-3a8b-ada8-9792dcc40af9",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "cladistiques"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "94d71cb2-ee17-3fc0-8fe0-b19c42089587",
                        "entry_id": "94ffef87-0412-3a8b-ada8-9792dcc40af9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Méthode de reconstruction phylogénétique permettant d’établir les relations de parenté entre organismes en identifiant des caractères dérivés partagés exclusifs (ou synapomorphies). Ces relations sont représentées sous forme de cladogramme, qui illustrent les groupes monophylétiques (ou clades) formés par ces organismes."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Biologie évolutive",
                            "Systématique",
                            "Phylogénie"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e74b0353-0064-420a-9f19-5624a4f01145",
                                "sense_id": "94d71cb2-ee17-3fc0-8fe0-b19c42089587",
                                "text": "La cladistique est une méthode de reconstruction phylogénétique élaborée dans les années 1950 par l’entomologiste allemand Willi Hennig."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "733ce5dd-ccbf-4a28-a751-48c62a5e2a1c",
                                "sense_id": "94d71cb2-ee17-3fc0-8fe0-b19c42089587",
                                "text": "Si les « natures simples » ne sont pas autre chose que les nœuds de la cladistique, elles vont ou bien devenir composantes du complexe ou bien être considérées à leur tour comme complexes au regard d’une autre nature plus simple."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fe2c02e9-03c2-4e5f-b72c-854960b8870e",
                        "source_entry_id": "94ffef87-0412-3a8b-ada8-9792dcc40af9",
                        "source_sense_id": "94d71cb2-ee17-3fc0-8fe0-b19c42089587",
                        "target_lang_word": "Kladistik",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Kladistik",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "93a501d4-8d08-35e5-8bb4-50997211fc8c",
                                        "entry_id": "a905e95c-5a32-3009-8313-d8adf115adfc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "wissenschaftliche Methodik der biologischen Systematik und Taxonomie auf der Basis der Evolutionsbiologie"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9ac43b62-5eb1-458d-be1c-fda3a7e25970",
                                                "sense_id": "93a501d4-8d08-35e5-8bb4-50997211fc8c",
                                                "text": "„Der Ausdruck „Kladistik“ für diese Methode, die auf der Verwendung von Kladen genannten geschlossenen Abstammungsgemeinschaften beruht, wurde ursprünglich von dem Evolutionsbiologen Ernst Mayr eingeführt, der damit die von Hennig selbst „phylogenetische Systematik“ genannte Methodik aber nicht neutral beschreiben, sondern kritisieren wollte.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b1b2b223-5014-4f02-8802-e70d5267a0b5",
                        "source_entry_id": "94ffef87-0412-3a8b-ada8-9792dcc40af9",
                        "source_sense_id": "94d71cb2-ee17-3fc0-8fe0-b19c42089587",
                        "target_lang_word": "cladistics",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "cladistics",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f5cc3393-2f18-371b-93ef-3642476ef5fe",
                                        "entry_id": "09e2b331-d0b7-34f5-999d-b5d5e61323c2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An approach to biological systematics in which organisms are grouped based upon synapomorphies (shared derived characteristics) only, and not upon symplesiomorphies (shared ancestral characteristics); a method of classifying organisms based on their evolutionary relationships instead of superficial characteristics."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "790ad880-1863-4646-8b47-26eb0842b5c9",
                                                "sense_id": "f5cc3393-2f18-371b-93ef-3642476ef5fe",
                                                "text": "Here we suggest emphasis on the techniques of cladistics (Eldredge and Cracraft 1980; Wiley 1981; Coddington 1988) because they provide a clear means of organizing phylogenetic information in branching diagrams."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "43140150-f3f0-4f76-8c2f-89662c8e44f6",
                                                "sense_id": "f5cc3393-2f18-371b-93ef-3642476ef5fe",
                                                "text": "The construction of branching patterns to map evolutionary change is called cladistics, and the devising of higher classifications (genus and up) to conform with the results of cladistics is called phylogenetic systematics.[…]Cladistics does allow us to judge which species are most likely to share a common ancestor, validating their placement in the same genus or family or higher taxon."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2ac89227-f3aa-4469-9a51-bfb632faa794",
                                                "sense_id": "f5cc3393-2f18-371b-93ef-3642476ef5fe",
                                                "text": "2001, Clare Bates Congdon, Gaphyl: A Genetic Algorithms Approach to Cladistics, Luc de Raedt, Arno Siebes (editors), Principles of Data Mining and Knowledge Discovery: 5th European Conference PKDD 2001, Volume 5, Springer, LNAI 2168, page 67,\nThis research investigates the use of genetic algorithms to solve problems from cladistics — a technique used by biologists to hypothesize the relationships between organisms."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
